WHY THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC

This repository is published so that the judges of the BLI Legal Tech Hackathon
2, and any other reader, can READ the source, reproduce the results described in
README.md, and evaluate the work. That is the entire purpose of the publication.

Beyond the rights set out below, the rights the GitHub Terms of Service confer
on Users of that service, and any right conferred by applicable law, no further
right is granted. Being publicly readable is not the same as being open source:
this repository carries no OSI-approved licence, and none is implied. That is a
deliberate decision, not an oversight.

PERMITTED

  1. Reading and consulting the source code and the documentation.
  2. Viewing and forking this repository within GitHub, to the extent the GitHub
     Terms of Service confer that right on Users of the service.
  3. Cloning or downloading the repository, and making the temporary technical
     copies strictly necessary to install its dependencies and run it locally,
     for the sole purpose of verifying the results stated in README.md and
     CURRENT_STATUS.md.
  4. Quoting short excerpts, with attribution, as permitted by applicable
     copyright law.

NOT PERMITTED without prior written permission from the copyright holder

Subject to the rights granted above, to the rights the GitHub Terms of Service
confer on Users of that service, and to any right conferred by applicable law:

  1. Republishing, mirroring or redistributing this repository, in whole or in
     part, otherwise than by forking it within GitHub.
  2. Modifying it, or creating derivative works from it.
  3. Incorporating it, in whole or in part, into any other project, product or
     service, whether commercial or not.
  4. Exploiting the content in any way beyond the limited verification permitted
     above.
  5. Using it to train, fine-tune, evaluate or benchmark a machine-learning
     model.

